# Backend Conventions

## Module System

Always use ES Modules. Include `.js` in every local import.

```js
// ✅
import User from "../models/user.model.js";
export const myController = async (req, res) => {};

// ❌ Never use require()
```

## Controller Shape

Every controller is `async`, uses try/catch, and returns a consistent JSON envelope.

```js
export const myController = async (req, res) => {
  try {
    // ...
    return res.status(200).json({ success: true, message: "Done", data });
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("myController:", error.message);
    return res.status(500).json({ success: false, message: "Internal error" });
  }
};
```

- Use `req.userId` as the authenticated user ID string (set by `isAuth`).
- Use `req.user` when you need the full decoded JWT object (e.g. `req.user._id`).
- **Never send `password`** in any response. Strip with `.select("-password")` or `user.password = undefined`.
- Always `return` on early responses to stop execution.

## Route Conventions

```js
// POST   /create-<resource>
// GET    /get-all-<resource>  |  /get-<resource>/:id  |  /profile/:param
// PUT    /update-<resource>
// DELETE /remove-<resource>/:id
// GET    /get-status/:id  (for status checks)
```

Protect every route that needs authentication: `router.get("/...", isAuth, controller)`.
Apply `upload` middleware before controllers that accept file uploads.

## Middleware Application Order

```js
// Pattern for file upload routes
router.put("/update-profile", isAuth, upload.fields([...]), controller);

// Pattern for post creation
router.post("/create-post", isAuth, upload.single("image"), controller);
```

`aiModeration` is available in `middlewares/aiModeration.js` (currently disabled in routes).
Enable by adding it before any controller that accepts `description`, `content`, or `aiPrompt`.

## Mongoose Models

All schemas use `{ timestamps: true }`. Named + default export:
```js
export const User = mongoose.model("User", userSchema);
export default User;
```

Use `$addToSet` to avoid duplicates in arrays; `$pull` to remove; `$push` to append.
Always `.populate()` only the fields you need:
```js
.populate("author", "firstName lastName profileImage headline userName")
```

## Real-time Emissions

```js
import { io } from "../index.js";               // broadcast or targeted emits
import { userSocketMap } from "../config/socket.js"; // userId → socketId map

// Targeted (private)
const sid = userSocketMap.get(userId.toString());
if (sid) io.to(sid).emit("statusUpdate", { updatedUserId, newStatus });

// Broadcast (all clients)
io.emit("likeUpdated", { postId, likes: post.like });
```

Always check `if (sid)` before targeted emits.

## Security Rules

- Passwords hashed with `bcrypt.hash(password, 10)` on signup. Compare with `bcrypt.compare`.
- JWT signed with `JWT_SECRET`, TTL 7 days. Use `genToken(user)` / `verifyToken(token)` from `config/genToken.js`.
- Cookie set as `httpOnly: false`, `secure: true` in production (`NODE_ENVIRONMENT === "production"`), `sameSite: "strict"`.
- CORS restricted to `http://localhost:5173` in development.
- Never log full error objects in production; log `error.message`.
